From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:51:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement wlr-data-control-unstable-v1

Add the zwlr_data_control_manager_v1 global (version 2). It lets a
client read and set the clipboard and the primary selection without
keyboard focus, which is what clipboard managers such as cliphist,
clipman and wl-clip-persist need.

Reading: every data-control device gets the current selection and
primary selection when it is created and again on every MetaSelection
owner change, as an offer carrying the owner's mime types. receive is
served with meta_selection_transfer_async(), like the offers of focused
clients. An offer that was replaced returns EOF instead of newer data.
The handler announces the current owner rather than the signal
argument, because the clipboard manager re-sets the owner from inside
the owner-changed emission that unsets it.

Setting: set_selection and set_primary_selection go through
meta_wayland_data_device_set_selection() and
meta_wayland_data_device_primary_set_selection() (now exported), so a
data-control source becomes the selection the same way a focused
client's source does, without the focus check. The last selection
serial is reused, so a focused client's next copy still takes over.
Setting NULL also clears an owner the data devices do not track, such
as the clipboard manager's saved copy. Sources send send/cancelled.
Reusing a source raises used_source, and offering after the source was
set raises invalid_offer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
